{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>May YHWH lift His face to you, etc.</b> The meaning: if deeds brought it about that they separated your sins between you and your Elohim — may YHWH, who separates, lift. <b>And may He establish peace for you</b> — the meaning is, this is the opposite of separation. And whoever contemplates the word שָׁלוֹם will know that it is the very foundation sustaining the upper worlds and the lower worlds, and it is the vessel that holds blessing when there is no separator — and this is the sod of ״וְשָׂמוּ אֶת שְׁמִי עַל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״, concerning which the Speaker concludes ״וַאֲנִי אֲבָרְכֵם״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:29.824729200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}